(276859, 18721, 5728, '<td valign="top">Choice capture. The motion blur on the wings works well especially contrasted against the sharp head.</td>', 'Choice capture. The motion blur on the wings works well especially contrasted against the sharp head.', '2003-04-24 09:16:51.000000', NULL, 1),
(276860, 18864, 5728, '<td valign="top">Awesome macro, all that pollen on the bee and the way he is greedily in the flower going for more gives this image impact!</td>', 'Awesome macro, all that pollen on the bee and the way he is greedily in the flower going for more gives this image impact!', '2003-04-24 09:17:43.000000', NULL, 1),
(276862, 19120, 5728, '<td valign="top">I like the layering effect in this image and also the fact that only the main subject is in focus. You did well!</td>', 'I like the layering effect in this image and also the fact that only the main subject is in focus. You did well!', '2003-04-24 09:18:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(276863, 18542, 5728, '<td valign="top">Cute! Good capture, you have a good eye. And patience!</td>', 'Cute! Good capture, you have a good eye. And patience!', '2003-04-24 09:19:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(276864, 18955, 7743, '<td valign="top">The foreground is exposed nicely but the background is way overexposed and takes up more than half the picture.  If this was done to get the horse nicely exposed  then the image could possibly be improved by including more ground and less sky and use spot metering on the horse.</td>', 'The foreground is exposed nicely but the background is way overexposed and takes up more than half the picture.  If this was done to get the horse nicely exposed  then the image could possibly be improved by including more ground and less sky and use spot metering on the horse.', '2003-04-24 09:19:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(276866, 18856, 5728, '<td valign="top">This is a very good macro, fantastic. The whole main subject is so detailed and sharp and lifted off the background by your shallow DOF. Well done!</td>', 'This is a very good macro, fantastic. The whole main subject is so detailed and sharp and lifted off the background by your shallow DOF. Well done!', '2003-04-24 09:20:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(276870, 18907, 7743, '<td valign="top">Exposure is good.  To get even more impact the image could have been cropped closer around the head on all sides except the left or more of the body could be included to balance the amount of sky.</td>', 'Exposure is good.  To get even more impact the image could have been cropped closer around the head on all sides except the left or more of the body could be included to balance the amount of sky.', '2003-04-24 09:22:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(276871, 18883, 7743, '<td valign="top">It appears that your light source has overexposed the foreground and has given the duck redeye.  The only suggestion I could make for this would be to reduce the power of the light source or back away.  Due to the subject matter, a longer exposure with no extra light source is not an option.</td>', 'It appears that your light source has overexposed the foreground and has given the duck redeye.  The only suggestion I could make for this would be to reduce the power of the light source or back away.  Due to the subject matter, a longer exposure with no extra light source is not an option.', '2003-04-24 09:27:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(276872, 19182, 2634, '<td valign="top">funny, funny title. No offense but(t) I wouldn''t want this for my wall!</td>', 'funny, funny title. No offense but(t) I wouldn''t want this for my wall!', '2003-04-24 09:27:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(276873, 18813, 5728, '<td valign="top">This is good! The composition is good with the butterfly in the lower left hand corner. The shallow DOF works well, although I would have tried for an even shallower DOF to blur the flowers at the lower left. They are a little distracting and compete with the butterfly.</td>', 'This is good! The composition is good with the butterfly in the lower left hand corner. The shallow DOF works well, although I would have tried for an even shallower DOF to blur the flowers at the lower left. They are a little distracting and compete with the butterfly.', '2003-04-24 09:29:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(276874, 19014, 5728, '<td valign="top">Everything is in focus in this pic which is necessary as a shallow DOF would have blurred the back duck. The composition is fairly good, everything is cropped evenly. Personally, I would have liked to have seen a little more of the reeds at the top, but that''s just me.</td>', 'Everything is in focus in this pic which is necessary as a shallow DOF would have blurred the back duck. The composition is fairly good, everything is cropped evenly. Personally, I would have liked to have seen a little more of the reeds at the top, but that''s just me.', '2003-04-24 09:32:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(276875, 18794, 7743, '<td valign="top">Nicely done.  The only thing I would suggest to improve the image would be to give the bee more space to fly into.</td>', 'Nicely done.  The only thing I would suggest to improve the image would be to give the bee more space to fly into.', '2003-04-24 09:33:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(276877, 19196, 5728, '<td valign="top">Were you patient and waited for this or did you train them? Anyway, it is an excellent capture with a fantastic composition. You did everything correctly with this image! The shallow DOF, the lighting, the focus, everything is bang on, congratulations on a top photo.</td>', 'Were you patient and waited for this or did you train them? Anyway, it is an excellent capture with a fantastic composition. You did everything correctly with this image! The shallow DOF, the lighting, the focus, everything is bang on, congratulations on a top photo.', '2003-04-24 09:33:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(276878, 18937, 5728, '<td valign="top">The lighting on the water creates an amazing effect which in turn makes for an excellent background. The bird is standing very majestically there, as if you ask it to pose for you like that. I like it, you did well here!</td>', 'The lighting on the water creates an amazing effect which in turn makes for an excellent background. The bird is standing very majestically there, as if you ask it to pose for you like that. I like it, you did well here!', '2003-04-24 09:35:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(276879, 18518, 7743, '<td valign="top">Your Heilin'' Coo is a little under exposed.  Spot metering on the cow may have helped.</td>', 'Your Heilin'' Coo is a little under exposed.  Spot metering on the cow may have helped.', '2003-04-24 09:36:09.000000', NULL, 1),
(276881, 18768, 7743, '<td valign="top">The depth of field seems a little shallow.  I don''t think there would be a problem with your subject getting away if you stopped down the lense (smaller aperture, larger number) and adjusted the shutter speed accordingly.  This would allow you to possibly get both attenae in focus.  Also change your vantage point could help with this as well.</td>', 'The depth of field seems a little shallow.  I don''t think there would be a problem with your subject getting away if you stopped down the lense (smaller aperture, larger number) and adjusted the shutter speed accordingly.  This would allow you to possibly get both attenae in focus.  Also change your vantage point could help with this as well.', '2003-04-24 09:42:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(276882, 19178, 7743, '<td valign="top">He/She looks defiant.</td>', 'He/She looks defiant.', '2003-04-24 09:44:46.000000', NULL, 1),
(276883, 18456, 7743, '<td valign="top">Depth of field seems to be slightly out of place.  The wasp''s forward attena is out of focus but part of the leaf behind the wasp is in focus.  Stepping back just a step (baby step)  would probably have helped here.</td>', 'Depth of field seems to be slightly out of place.  The wasp''s forward attena is out of focus but part of the leaf behind the wasp is in focus.  Stepping back just a step (baby step)  would probably have helped here.', '2003-04-24 09:48:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(276884, 18295, 7743, '<td valign="top">He seems to be leaning to the left.  Was the ground sloped?</td>', 'He seems to be leaning to the left.  Was the ground sloped?', '2003-04-24 09:51:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(276887, 19004, 7743, '<td valign="top">A different vantage point, such as at duck level, could possibly give this photo more impact and appeal.</td>', 'A different vantage point, such as at duck level, could possibly give this photo more impact and appeal.', '2003-04-24 09:58:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(276889, 18591, 7743, '<td valign="top">This is a tough challenge.  All of your subjects are very dark and fill about 1/3 of the image.  If you used an averge metering method, which I suspect since the foreground and background are nicely exposed, your subjects will be under exposed.  One solution here would be to use a different vantage point to eliminate some of the bright background and spot meter on the area you want to expose for.  Also, using and ND or polarizing filter might help.</td>', 'This is a tough challenge.  All of your subjects are very dark and fill about 1/3 of the image.  If you used an averge metering method, which I suspect since the foreground and background are nicely exposed, your subjects will be under exposed.  One solution here would be to use a different vantage point to eliminate some of the bright background and spot meter on the area you want to expose for.  Also, using and ND or polarizing filter might help.', '2003-04-24 10:11:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(276890, 18884, 7743, '<td valign="top">Cropping a little less on the bottom (to get the complete reflection) and less on the left (to give the goose somewhere to go) would give this image more impact.  As far as exposure goes it seems to be slightly overexposed.</td>', 'Cropping a little less on the bottom (to get the complete reflection) and less on the left (to give the goose somewhere to go) would give this image more impact.  As far as exposure goes it seems to be slightly overexposed.', '2003-04-24 10:14:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(276891, 19164, 3569, '<td valign="top">Try a black vulture, turkeys have red heads.</td>', 'Try a black vulture, turkeys have red heads.', '2003-04-24 10:14:51.000000', NULL, 1),
