(282292, 18511, 1005, '<td valign="top">Cute bunny rabbits!  First, the cage - unfortunate, unavoidable but nasty.  The glare at the rear of the frame, also nasty.  Little detail of the rabbits is viewable.  Maybe try this from the other side of the farther rabbit (would at least cut out some of the glare).  6 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Cute bunny rabbits!  First, the cage - unfortunate, unavoidable but nasty.  The glare at the rear of the frame, also nasty.  Little detail of the rabbits is viewable.  Maybe try this from the other side of the farther rabbit (would at least cut out some of the glare).  6 Rob the Swash', '2003-04-29 17:47:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(282297, 18865, 1005, '<td valign="top">Cute scene!  Dogs love to chase birds!!  The seagull is pretty good (but not crystal sharp), the dog is mostly a dog shaped blob, esp. sillhouetted as it is.  The far background seems hazy, too.  Fun shot, but 6 score.  Rob the Swash</td>', 'Cute scene!  Dogs love to chase birds!!  The seagull is pretty good (but not crystal sharp), the dog is mostly a dog shaped blob, esp. sillhouetted as it is.  The far background seems hazy, too.  Fun shot, but 6 score.  Rob the Swash', '2003-04-29 17:53:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(282299, 18833, 1005, '<td valign="top">Nice scene (would have worked for the Weather Challenge, too!)  Focus seems more on the city and the weather than the cows, they seem less than sharp, as if foreground materiel.  Focus down at the cows, hold the focal lock, then look up more.  6 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Nice scene (would have worked for the Weather Challenge, too!)  Focus seems more on the city and the weather than the cows, they seem less than sharp, as if foreground materiel.  Focus down at the cows, hold the focal lock, then look up more.  6 Rob the Swash', '2003-04-29 17:58:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(282301, 19017, 1005, '<td valign="top">Pretty horsey!  It''s a bit of a small image and the open area seems as if it is ?glare?<br/>6 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Pretty horsey!  It''s a bit of a small image and the open area seems as if it is ?glare?6 Rob the Swash', '2003-04-29 18:02:11.000000', NULL, 1),
(282302, 19123, 3669, '<td valign="top">This is a good attempt at a still action shot.  However, the entire bird is blurry.  A faster shutter speed would take the blurr out.  Do you have manual controls on your camera.   If you have sufficient light on your subject (here, the bird appears to be in the shadow of the trees, so there might not be), you can increase your shutter speed to stop the action, but you let in less light.  I\''m assuming that by being a beginner to photography that you might have been in automatic mode.  If so, the camera adjusted itself to the lack of light by lowering the shutter speed, thereby causing the bird to be blurred in the course of his flight.  Even if the bird\''s wings are blurred, the photo would be more effective if it\''s head, tail and legs were more in focus.  By the way, I like the reflection of the bird in the water at the bottom of the picture.  I hope this helps...I\''m kind of a beginner myself, so someone with more experience could probably explain it better.</td>', 'This is a good attempt at a still action shot.  However, the entire bird is blurry.  A faster shutter speed would take the blurr out.  Do you have manual controls on your camera.   If you have sufficient light on your subject (here, the bird appears to be in the shadow of the trees, so there might not be), you can increase your shutter speed to stop the action, but you let in less light.  I\''m assuming that by being a beginner to photography that you might have been in automatic mode.  If so, the camera adjusted itself to the lack of light by lowering the shutter speed, thereby causing the bird to be blurred in the course of his flight.  Even if the bird\''s wings are blurred, the photo would be more effective if it\''s head, tail and legs were more in focus.  By the way, I like the reflection of the bird in the water at the bottom of the picture.  I hope this helps...I\''m kind of a beginner myself, so someone with more experience could probably explain it better.', '2003-04-29 18:02:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(282303, 18298, 1005, '<td valign="top">Cute title (w/o it I would have had to ask "where is the fauna?")  Subjects are not very detailed, esp. this far away.  Other than the title/joke, it''s kinda hard to "get behind" this photo.  6 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Cute title (w/o it I would have had to ask "where is the fauna?")  Subjects are not very detailed, esp. this far away.  Other than the title/joke, it''s kinda hard to "get behind" this photo.  6 Rob the Swash', '2003-04-29 18:03:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(282304, 18816, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very cute sheep and sheepettes!  Focus seems a bit indeterminate, could be the glare off their white/white faces.  Maybe white balancing their faces (or the little guy''s hind quarters) would have lowered the glarish look.  Cute little devils!<br/>6 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very cute sheep and sheepettes!  Focus seems a bit indeterminate, could be the glare off their white/white faces.  Maybe white balancing their faces (or the little guy''s hind quarters) would have lowered the glarish look.  Cute little devils!6 Rob the Swash', '2003-04-29 18:06:03.000000', NULL, 1),
(282306, 18650, 1005, '<td valign="top">It''s a bug!  I know you didn''t have a lot of lighting control, but the issues around this photo are mostly lighting related.  The head is too shadowed, the rear is overly glarish.  Clarity is good, where the lighting allows it.  6 Rob the Swash</td>', 'It''s a bug!  I know you didn''t have a lot of lighting control, but the issues around this photo are mostly lighting related.  The head is too shadowed, the rear is overly glarish.  Clarity is good, where the lighting allows it.  6 Rob the Swash', '2003-04-29 18:07:55.000000', NULL, 1),
