(282687, 18556, 7151, '<td valign="top">Way to go, Bud!!!  Congrats, this is a great shot.  You''ve taken your place as master of the A40!  ;-)</td>', 'Way to go, Bud!!!  Congrats, this is a great shot.  You''ve taken your place as master of the A40!  ;-)', '2003-04-30 01:54:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(282721, 18751, 2923, '<td valign="top">Thanks Journey.  I think you''d be surprised that this is a crop -- yes, i am whoring in this challenge :) and a VERY tight crop indeed, almost no resizing needed, seriously.<br/> <br/>I did several crops of this scene and use this the best, then just add a bit of saturation (Channel Mixer to minimize noises -- if you use saturation button in PS it adds a lot more noises).  That''s why the edges of the stem is sort of blurry because i am losing resolution big time.<br/> <br/>It was shot with a 50 mm lens too....  just cropped.  The original photo had the bee as the focus @ F2.5 so i know most of the flowers will be OOF outside the plane, hand held, was going to do a FLORA photo and turned it to a Fauna challenge.<br/> <br/>Too bad this will not be able to be "printed" as it is a very very very small crop of the original photo and doens''t have enough resolution.  It''s funny how a lot of people "believed" it''s a macro when it''s really just a large photo cropped down tightly.<br/> <br/>Oh yeah, i do have that 70-200 mm L lens :)  but it''s not suitable for macros.  Probably could''ve used it to get closer than what the original photo was... but it''s not a macro lens -- they both have the 100 mm macro.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-04-30 01:12:37.</i></td>', 'Thanks Journey.  I think you''d be surprised that this is a crop -- yes, i am whoring in this challenge :) and a VERY tight crop indeed, almost no resizing needed, seriously. I did several crops of this scene and use this the best, then just add a bit of saturation (Channel Mixer to minimize noises -- if you use saturation button in PS it adds a lot more noises).  That''s why the edges of the stem is sort of blurry because i am losing resolution big time. It was shot with a 50 mm lens too....  just cropped.  The original photo had the bee as the focus @ F2.5 so i know most of the flowers will be OOF outside the plane, hand held, was going to do a FLORA photo and turned it to a Fauna challenge. Too bad this will not be able to be "printed" as it is a very very very small crop of the original photo and doens''t have enough resolution.  It''s funny how a lot of people "believed" it''s a macro when it''s really just a large photo cropped down tightly. Oh yeah, i do have that 70-200 mm L lens :)  but it''s not suitable for macros.  Probably could''ve used it to get closer than what the original photo was... but it''s not a macro lens -- they both have the 100 mm macro.', '2003-04-30 02:06:41.000000', '2003-04-30 02:12:37.000000', 0),
(282739, 18622, 7994, '<td valign="top">The original image was 24mb in size.  So, while resizing for the web the quality got lost.</td>', 'The original image was 24mb in size.  So, while resizing for the web the quality got lost.', '2003-04-30 02:12:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(282743, 18923, 6804, '<td valign="top">Thanks for the vote of confidence you guys, I watched the score on this one just keep dropping, I really thought it would do MUCH better than it did. I liked this one WAY better than my flora shot at 5th place, go-figure??<br/> <br/>The original on this is a much wider view of this shot. I cropped it down to add detail and ..wellinterest, I thought ha ha ha.  The monkey in the background is actually in the mist from a waterfall just to his right. ---- I guess it does look a lot like dust.    OH WELL. I had fun and I LOVE a lot of the other shots in this challenge.<br/></td>', 'Thanks for the vote of confidence you guys, I watched the score on this one just keep dropping, I really thought it would do MUCH better than it did. I liked this one WAY better than my flora shot at 5th place, go-figure?? The original on this is a much wider view of this shot. I cropped it down to add detail and ..wellinterest, I thought ha ha ha.  The monkey in the background is actually in the mist from a waterfall just to his right. ---- I guess it does look a lot like dust.    OH WELL. I had fun and I LOVE a lot of the other shots in this challenge.', '2003-04-30 02:14:23.000000', NULL, 0),
(282814, 18556, 6565, '<td valign="top">Sorry, my earlier comment was incomplete -- I meant Shrek because of the texture being so clean in your photo, it almost looks like computer graphics!  The crispness of the foreground really works against a hazy background.  Congratulations on your win, it was well-deserved! :)</td>', 'Sorry, my earlier comment was incomplete -- I meant Shrek because of the texture being so clean in your photo, it almost looks like computer graphics!  The crispness of the foreground really works against a hazy background.  Congratulations on your win, it was well-deserved! :)', '2003-04-30 02:44:49.000000', NULL, 0),
