(282962, 19064, 1176, '<td valign="top">Wow, I''m flatered.<br/>This is a pure snapshot, took around 20 pics of the birds surrounding the boat while we were throwing fish scraps of it.<br/>Only post edit I did was the great Auto Color in PS 7 (ctrl+shift+b)<br/>For those of you who think it is fake, you can look at the <a href="//finnur.nord.is/?dir=grasleppa%2F&amp;startpic=36" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">whole series</a> from my travel to the north of Iceland. (In icelandic)<br/> <br/>Thanks all for great comments and your wotes.</td>', 'Wow, I''m flatered.This is a pure snapshot, took around 20 pics of the birds surrounding the boat while we were throwing fish scraps of it.Only post edit I did was the great Auto Color in PS 7 (ctrl+shift+b)For those of you who think it is fake, you can look at the whole series from my travel to the north of Iceland. (In icelandic) Thanks all for great comments and your wotes.', '2003-04-30 07:12:17.000000', NULL, 0),
(282987, 18699, 7187, '<td valign="top">This is my son''s "pet" scorpion, named "Scorpion", of course.  I just shined a bright light on her(??) and she had a blue-ish tint.  She''s actually black, but the bright light made her look blue.</td>', 'This is my son''s "pet" scorpion, named "Scorpion", of course.  I just shined a bright light on her(??) and she had a blue-ish tint.  She''s actually black, but the bright light made her look blue.', '2003-04-30 07:56:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(282989, 18556, 5250, '<td valign="top">The texture and colours on this are just fantastic! Congrats!</td>', 'The texture and colours on this are just fantastic! Congrats!', '2003-04-30 07:57:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(282990, 18703, 7365, '<td valign="top">This crocodile is actually a crocodile head that my sister-in-law bought from Florida for my son.  I put it outside in my back yard and took a pic at an angle that made it look more realistic.</td>', 'This crocodile is actually a crocodile head that my sister-in-law bought from Florida for my son.  I put it outside in my back yard and took a pic at an angle that made it look more realistic.', '2003-04-30 07:59:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(283002, 19180, 2221, '<td valign="top">Focus, focus, focus. It''s always the same people complain about ;-) I liked the fuzziness.<br/>I understand that the "Pi" connection couldn''t be understood by many, but I thought that the image would be interesting to some more people. Seems that I was wrong. :-/<br/> <br/>Anyway, thanks to the people who commented and said that they like the photo.<br/> <br/> <br/>P.S.: As described in the photographers comments, the image is colour inverted and not infrared.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2003-04-30 07:18:28.</i></td>', 'Focus, focus, focus. It''s always the same people complain about ;-) I liked the fuzziness.I understand that the "Pi" connection couldn''t be understood by many, but I thought that the image would be interesting to some more people. Seems that I was wrong. :-/ Anyway, thanks to the people who commented and said that they like the photo.  P.S.: As described in the photographers comments, the image is colour inverted and not infrared.', '2003-04-30 08:15:20.000000', '2003-04-30 08:18:28.000000', 0),
(283010, 18728, 8023, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everyone for their comments.  They are the reason I started submitting my photos.  I agree with the majority of people who suggested cropping out the water-it would have made the photo much better.  I''ve implemented some cropping in my transportation selection-can''t wait to see what everyone thinks of that submission.</td>', 'Thanks to everyone for their comments.  They are the reason I started submitting my photos.  I agree with the majority of people who suggested cropping out the water-it would have made the photo much better.  I''ve implemented some cropping in my transportation selection-can''t wait to see what everyone thinks of that submission.', '2003-04-30 08:27:31.000000', NULL, 0),
(283015, 18526, 472, '<td valign="top">LOVE this guy''s face and expression.  So benign, yet comical.  Still makes me chuckle to look at :)</td>', 'LOVE this guy''s face and expression.  So benign, yet comical.  Still makes me chuckle to look at :)', '2003-04-30 08:35:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(283022, 18866, 5158, '<td valign="top">Thanx for all the nice comments.<br/>This tiny snail was going up one of our trees and it was the first shot I took of it. I then tried to place it better, but it feelt down in the grass and I couldn''t find it again.<br/>Later I collected some of these baby snail and tried to do a indoor shoot of one climbing allong some grass, but it didn''t work: they were just too fast!!<br/>That''s true: they came only out at low light conditions and then they moved to fast for the slow shutter speed. In bright light they tend to stay in the house.<br/>So I gave up and submitted the first shot, knowing that it had some focus problems.<br/> <br/>Jörg</td>', 'Thanx for all the nice comments.This tiny snail was going up one of our trees and it was the first shot I took of it. I then tried to place it better, but it feelt down in the grass and I couldn''t find it again.Later I collected some of these baby snail and tried to do a indoor shoot of one climbing allong some grass, but it didn''t work: they were just too fast!!That''s true: they came only out at low light conditions and then they moved to fast for the slow shutter speed. In bright light they tend to stay in the house.So I gave up and submitted the first shot, knowing that it had some focus problems. Jörg', '2003-04-30 08:46:02.000000', NULL, 0),
