(283847, 18365, 7106, '<td valign="top">No, the owl isn''t real. This dissapoints me again. People rated it down because they assume that it has to be a living animal. It did not say in the challenge rules that it had to be living. <br/> <br/>Thank you for thoes of you that made actual comments that are helpful. Not stuff like  "w/ real effort you could have found a real owl," or "Ummm, I don''t think the challenge met fake animals. Major points off for that, however above that, the "owl" is well lit in this picture and it''s nicely focused."  But I''m glad that you did comment instead of just rating it. <br/> <br/>I dislike how people just assume what they think the challenge means witout really reading it. I guess there is no way around that though.</td>', 'No, the owl isn''t real. This dissapoints me again. People rated it down because they assume that it has to be a living animal. It did not say in the challenge rules that it had to be living.  Thank you for thoes of you that made actual comments that are helpful. Not stuff like  "w/ real effort you could have found a real owl," or "Ummm, I don''t think the challenge met fake animals. Major points off for that, however above that, the "owl" is well lit in this picture and it''s nicely focused."  But I''m glad that you did comment instead of just rating it.  I dislike how people just assume what they think the challenge means witout really reading it. I guess there is no way around that though.', '2003-04-30 16:49:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(283893, 18905, 1863, '<td valign="top">Great photo. I didn''t have time to vote during the challenge, but I had this pegged as a top 3. I think you were underrated because of all the bird/pond type bird shots in the challenge. I just love this, and it''s going into my favorites!<br/>-da</td>', 'Great photo. I didn''t have time to vote during the challenge, but I had this pegged as a top 3. I think you were underrated because of all the bird/pond type bird shots in the challenge. I just love this, and it''s going into my favorites!-da', '2003-04-30 17:21:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(283898, 18751, 656, '<td valign="top">This is a cool shot - great detail on the bee - though the saturation is hurting my eyes :)<br/> <br/>Btw ,the 70-200L _is_ a great lens for doing close-up work...  Just because it doesn''t say macro, doesn''t mean it can''t be used (I have an entire book on macro photography that only mentions macro lenses for about 4 pages)  I''ve taken some nice macro of flowers with it.<br/> <br/><a href="//www.pbase.com/gordonmcgregor/spring" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">All 70-200 lens for the close-ups</a></td>', 'This is a cool shot - great detail on the bee - though the saturation is hurting my eyes :) Btw ,the 70-200L _is_ a great lens for doing close-up work...  Just because it doesn''t say macro, doesn''t mean it can''t be used (I have an entire book on macro photography that only mentions macro lenses for about 4 pages)  I''ve taken some nice macro of flowers with it. All 70-200 lens for the close-ups', '2003-04-30 17:25:58.000000', NULL, 0),
